From 5a5732751374a51bc2637a0593298a5baf42abf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:24:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: add uhf_service to the new_objects ignore list for
 API 29-33

Real build failure, found by actually running the build after the
previous commit's fixes got past sepolicy_freeze_test and
fuzzer_bindings_test:

  SELinux: The following public types were found added to the policy
  without an entry into the compatibility mapping file(s) found in
  private/compat/V.v/V.v[.ignore].cil, where V.v is the latest API level.
  uhf_service

treble_sepolicy_tests_{29,30,31,32,33}.0 all failed with this. Every
public type has to be reachable from every older API level's
compatibility mapping, either by mapping it to something that existed
back then, or - for a type with no analogue in that older policy, which
uhf_service is - by listing it in that level's new_objects ignore set,
exactly the mechanism ondevicepersonalization_system_service,
uwb_service, and usb_serial_device already use in these same files for
the same reason. Added uhf_service alongside them in all five
29.0.ignore.cil through 33.0.ignore.cil files (there is no 34.0 compat
directory - 34.0 is this tree's current/unfrozen level, so it needs no
self-mapping).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
